From: koalabuttz <27229333+koalabuttz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: read the last lod distance through lodInfo

XModelGetLodOutDist() returned a float at parentList + 28 bytes per
lod. With four-byte pointers that is lodInfo[numLods - 1].dist (lodInfo
starts 28 bytes after parentList and an XModelLodInfo is 28 bytes). It
now names the field, so it no longer depends on the pointer size.

No behaviour change in the 32-bit build.
---
 src/xanim/xmodel_utils.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/xanim/xmodel_utils.cpp b/src/xanim/xmodel_utils.cpp
index 802e19af..ef001bf4 100644
--- a/src/xanim/xmodel_utils.cpp
+++ b/src/xanim/xmodel_utils.cpp
@@ -76,7 +76,7 @@ int __cdecl XModelGetNumLods(const XModel *model)
 
 double __cdecl XModelGetLodOutDist(const XModel *model)
 {
-    return *((float *)&model->parentList + 7 * XModelGetNumLods(model));
+    return model->lodInfo[XModelGetNumLods(model) - 1].dist;
 }
 
 int __cdecl XModelNumBones(const XModel *model)
